From 592079506b351d9c70a1613bf628f1c44adc85aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WGS Extract AI <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:40:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] postprocess_variants: call one contig at a time
 (wgsextract #647)

It parsed every CallVariantsOutput up front and held them, their groups
and every called variant until the end: a whole genome's ~8M sites needed
tens of GB (0.63 GB for chr20 alone). It now keeps the records serialized
(~16x smaller), then parses, calls, resolves and writes one contig at a
time, in reference order, so memory follows the largest contig. Haplotype
resolution only joins overlapping variants, which share a contig. Records
at one position keep a stable order. chr20's VCF is byte-identical.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
